# Signed PDF fixtures are BYTES, not text.
#
# `tools/parity/fixtures/seal/*.pdf` are the inputs the seal goldens were
# computed over, and a PDF signature covers byte ranges of the file itself.
# Any end-of-line conversion shifts every offset after the first newline and
# changes the bytes the signature is over, so a converted fixture does not
# merely differ - it makes a valid signature read as tampered.
#
# It would have gone unnoticed for a while: these files contain only LF, so
# committing them is a no-op, CI checks out on Linux where nothing converts,
# and only a Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf would have
# rewritten them - failing nine goldens on one developer's machine and nowhere
# else.
*.pdf -text

# Everything else a parity fixture might hold, for the same reason.
tools/parity/fixtures/** -text
